        "The corrected construction uses \\(M\\), so both the formula and the complete definition metadata must be replaced atomically.",
        "correct: The robust interval is intersected with the known parameter range \\([-2M,2M]\\), but the frozen Gaussian comparator is not. An explicit witness is \\(d=1\\), \\(A\\sim\\operatorname{Bernoulli}(1/2)\\), \\(Y(1)=M+Z\\), and \\(Y(0)=-M+Z\\), where \\(Z\\) is an independent symmetric \\(\\{ -\\sigma,\\sigma\\}\\)-valued variable with \\(0<\\sigma\\le M\\). Then \\(\\tau(P)=2M\\) and \\(V_{\\mathrm{eff}}(P)=4\\sigma^2\\); whenever this variance lies in the declared band, the unprojected Gaussian upper endpoint has a nonvanishing root-\\(n\\) excess over \\(2M\\), whereas the robust upper endpoint is at most \\(2M\\). Intersecting the comparator with the same range is the minimal formula correction, and projection is one-Lipschitz."
